# B&B optimization example for structural-order.
# A four-vertex clique needs four registers, but only three are available.
# Clique-first ordering exposes the contradiction before branching on the
# isolated vertices.
# Run from the repository root.
# Enabled:  ./build-clang-modules/pbqp --solve=bnb -Werror -O0 --numthreads=1 --timeout=0.7 -fstructural-order examples/pbqp/individual/bnb-structural-order.pbqp
# Baseline: ./build-clang-modules/pbqp --solve=bnb -Werror -O0 --numthreads=1 --timeout=0.7 -fno-structural-order examples/pbqp/individual/bnb-structural-order.pbqp
# Observed with Clang 21 Release on Intel Core Ultra X7 358H.
# Median elapsed CLI time over five alternating runs, including startup.
# Enabled: 7.4 ms, 5/5 infeasible.
# Baseline: 707.2 ms, 5/5 timeout.

PBQP 2
NODES 32
EDGES 6
MATRICES 1
NODE 0 4 INF 0 0 0
NODE 1 4 INF 0 0 0
NODE 2 4 INF 0 0 0
NODE 3 4 INF 0 0 0
NODE 4 4 INF 0 0 0
NODE 5 4 INF 0 0 0
